    <div class="card">
      <h2>Powers practice</h2>
      <p>
        This drill generates small exponent problems (base^exponent) —
        useful for anyone who needs quick recall of powers for exams,
        estimation, or programming-adjacent mental math, where reaching
        for a calculator every time is slower than knowing the value
        outright.
      </p>
      <p>
        There's no single universal shortcut for arbitrary powers the way
        there is for squares or cubes, so this is largely a recall drill —
        though breaking a power down into repeated squaring (e.g. treating
        4th powers as "square, then square again") can make the
        calculation faster to verify by hand.
      </p>
